==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|āreola|small vacant space, garden}}

[[File:Weibliche brust en.jpg|right|thumb|A woman's breasts, with the areola indicated.]]
===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl2=areolae|pl3=areolæ}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} The colored [[circle]] around a [[nipple]], more exactly known as [[areola mammae]].
# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} Any small circular area that is different from its immediate environment such as the colored ring around the [[pupil]] of the [[eye]] ([[iris]]) or an inflamed region surrounding a [[pimple]].

====Usage notes====
* Not to be confused with {{term|aureola|lang=en}}.

